- **[Scrolling and input]** Root element scroll applies to the viewport per CSS overflow propagation (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:27-31; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:271-282), and the root element does not clip its own overflow (packages/blitz-paint/src/render.rs:349-358); viewport scroll offset lives on `NodeTree` (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:41-43); `overflow: hidden` axes are scrollable programmatically but not by the user (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:57-66; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:480-484); user scrolls chain unconsumed delta to the viewport, a `scroll_to` or a `scroll_by` clamps to one scroller and chains nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:176-192; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:547-582), and `scroll_into_view` writes every scrolling box on its target's containing-block chain, innermost first, and then the viewport — each nested write an instant `scroll_to` clamped to its own box, the requested behaviour applying to the viewport alone, so an into-view scroll never animates a nested box (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:655-734; ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07: the method itself is widened for every document, no second method beside it — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md); a box's client rect is the box's own — the shared bounds reader subtracts the scroll offset of every box on the containing-block chain above a node and never the node's own — and a hit stops at the padding box of every box paint clips — one that clips by `overflow`, on one axis or both, or one whose computed `contain` includes `paint` on a box paint applies it to (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — the root element excepted (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:2477-2504; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/writing_mode.rs:371-412; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:1437-1567;
 the founder's ruling, 2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer: both fixed in the engine, each a direct change for every document, ahead of the MCP surface; how far each reaches — the fix made in the shared reader, the stop at paint's overflow half — is the operator's answer of that day, and the second reader `Node::absolute_position` subtracts only its containing blocks' scroll offsets (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18; §Standard Contracts → Scrolling, selection, tree); both are flagged upstreamable, cut against upstream `main` at 7832c177, and no upstream pull request is open — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/report.md); a third direct engine change for every document stands beside those two since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, in the accessibility builder's own file: the builder writes AccessKit's `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on an element's node from `aria-selected`, `aria-pressed` and `aria-invalid`, read by value (a select's option excepted, its `selected` its chosen state, [DOM semantics]) — `toggled` from `aria-checked` in place of `aria-pressed` on a checkable role, and from neither on a native checkbox or radio (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) (§Standard Contracts → Mutation, query and CSSOM)
 — ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать», the English wording is the overseer's: the builder writes the three states on the node, and what an assistive technology reads of them stays unmeasured until the windowed check), flagged upstreamable against the same 7832c177, where `accessibility.rs` reads +57 −1 against that ref and read +26 −0 before the chunk (the local ref, not fetched), and no upstream pull request is open (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:169-213 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md); a fifth direct engine change for every document stands beside the three this decision counts and the password paint under [Painting] since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, the range interaction model: an `input` whose `type` reads `range` (ASCII case-insensitive) holds its current value apart from its `value` attribute (`RangeInputData`, §Standard Contracts → Nodes and widgets), its rules written against the WHATWG range state in `node/range.rs` — `min` 0 and `max` 100 by default, a `max` below `min` reading `min`, `step` 1 by default, a step ≤ 0 or unparsable reading 1 and `any` setting no grid, the step base `min`, else the `value` attribute, else 0, the default value the midpoint, and every value sanitized to `[min, max]` and the nearest grid value, the greater on a tie (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:67-75; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:85-206); focused and with no `disabled` attribute (presence), `ArrowRight` and `ArrowUp` step it up, `ArrowLeft` and `ArrowDown` step it down, `Home` and `End` take it to its minimum and maximum, and every other key does nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:102-107; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:146-163);
 a main-button pointerdown sets the value from the hit's fraction of the content box, clamped to [0, 1], a box of no width reading 0, and a click focuses it and changes no value, so a label's synthetic click focuses without moving it (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:449-453; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:650-661; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:509-511; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:663-678; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:765-777); each change fires one `input` event and a move that changes nothing fires none (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:333-354); a `value` write re-seeds the current value and a `min`, `max` or `step` write or removal re-sanitizes it — a departure from the spec's dirty-value flag, the cost the founder's first fork answer took on so that a Dioxus re-render keeps control (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:361-367; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:388-390; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:525-532); form submission sends the formatted current value (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:334-335); before it no key or click moved a range input and a click did not focus it (measured at 2026-10-07-act-by-id) — ratified by the founder: his ruling of 2026-10-07 «Пусть будет а», his answers to the three forks of 2026-10-13 «Отдельное текущее значение», «Стрелки + Home/End (Рекомендую)» and «Клик даёт фокус (Рекомендую)», and his confirm of the wrap's answer card the same day «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)», which also covers the three consequences the operator confirmed at the review (submission sends the current value, a `value` write resets it, the pointerdown moves the value and the click focuses) — each by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label, the English wording the overseer's;
 flagged upstreamable against upstream `main` at 434e0661, which has no range interaction, and no upstream pull request is open; its merge surface is `node/element.rs`, `node/mod.rs`, `layout/construct.rs`, `mutator.rs`, `events/keyboard.rs`, `events/pointer.rs` and `form.rs`, with the new `node/range.rs`, read at upstream `main` `e72650a6` on 2026-10-15, three commits past that base, and untouched by upstream since it — `git diff --stat 434e0661 e72650a6` over it empty, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/evidence/merge-surface.md — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-range-input-interaction/report.md; at upstream `main` `f9cbb2756` upstream's taken hunks reach `node/element.rs`, `node/mod.rs`, `layout/construct.rs` and `mutator.rs`, the one conflict `construct.rs`'s import list, resolved to upstream's list plus `RangeInputData` (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-24-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship/evidence/take.md); three more direct engine changes for every document stand beside those since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, the sixth to the eighth: keyboard activation — a pressed `Enter` whose target is the focused node, after the text-input and range arms, dispatches a Click on it when it is no disabled form control ([DOM semantics]) and is a `button`, a `summary`, an `input` of type `submit`, `reset` or `button`, or an `a` with `href`, and a released Space on the focused node dispatches the same Click, through the new `handle_key_up`, for a `button`, a `summary`, or an `input` of type `submit`, `reset`, `button`, `checkbox` or `radio` that is not disabled — a link takes no Space, and a text input and a range input take neither key there — the Click's data built from `Node::synthetic_click_event_data(modifiers)` and queued by the event driver, so the app's handlers run before the default action `handle_click` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:114-119; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:124-144; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:202-217; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:219-233; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:235-245;
 §Standard Contracts → Events), so Enter and Space reach form submission, link navigation and `summary` toggling in every document, remote pages included (security-plan §Input Validation); a click focuses a button — `handle_click`'s submit arm became a button arm that matches a `button` of any type or an `input` of type `submit`, `reset` or `button`, focuses it through `generate_focus_events` / `set_focus_to`, then submits the form owner for a submit button and ends the walk matched, where before a submit button submitted without breaking the walk and every other button fell through to the unmatched clear of focus; a disabled form control still stops the walk first, a `disabled` attribute on any other element not, a click on a `select` focuses it through its own arm of the walk (below), and a click on any other element still clears focus (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:909-921; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:984-1001); and focusability reads `disabled` by presence ([DOM semantics]), on a form control alone (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — each answered by the founder himself at the chunk's forks, by question dialog in the overseer session on 2026-10-13, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option labels «Клавиши нажимают (Рекомендую)», «Клик даёт фокус (Рекомендую)» and «По наличию (Рекомендую)», and his confirm of the wrap's answer card on 2026-10-14 «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)», the English wording the overseer's; flagged upstreamable against upstream `main` at 434e0661, and no upstream pull request is open; their merge surface is `events/keyboard.rs`, `events/mod.rs`, `events/pointer.rs` and `node/element.rs`, read at upstream `main` `e72650a6` on 2026-10-15, three commits past that base, and untouched by upstream since it
 — `git diff --stat 434e0661 e72650a6` over it empty, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/evidence/merge-surface.md — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness/report.md; at upstream `main` `f9cbb2756` upstream's taken hunks reach `node/element.rs`, with no conflict (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-24-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship/evidence/take.md); a user scroll aborts a smooth scroll (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:424-426; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:135-139); smooth scrolls last 300 ms, cubic ease-in-out (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:112-122; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:432-433); fling decelerates 0.95 per 60 fps frame and stops below 0.1 (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:870-884), velocity from the last 100 ms of pan samples, doubled (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:110-151); wheel line deltas × 20 (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:1009-1012); drags start beyond 2 px (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:218-222); repeated clicks within 500 ms and 2 px, read on the document's clock (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:390-400); platform action modifier `META` on macOS (`SUPER` until keyboard-types 0.8, merged at the 2026-10-17 upstream sync), `CONTROL` elsewhere (packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:7-10); fragment-only link changes scroll in page (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:885-898; packages/blitz-dom/src/url.rs:23-31); empty or unmatched `top` fragments scroll to top (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:816-820)

- **Tests:** unit tests in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the end of the source file (apps/browser/src/about_pages.rs:200-201; apps/browser/src/browser_history.rs:166-167; apps/browser/src/favicon.rs:70-72; apps/browser/src/url_suggestions.rs:339-340; apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:310-311; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:609-610; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1520-1521; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3154-3155; packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs:525-526; packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:180-181; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/scrollbar.rs:224-237; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:1071-1205; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:2078-2164; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/fuzzy.rs:138-140; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/js_wrapper.rs:106-108; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/harness_test.rs:286-292; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/mod.rs:402-404); eight unit-test modules sit in files of their own, each a `#[cfg(test)]` child declared through `#[path]` at its parent — dioxus-native-dom's bridge tests, declared at the end of `dioxus_document.rs` as `#[cfg(test)] #[path = "dioxus_document_tests.rs"] mod bridge_tests;`, a child of the module under test so they reach its private fields with no constructor, `pub` or `cfg(test)` shim added (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:782-784), and, since 2026-10-16-file-splits, blitz-dom's `document::changed_set_tests` and `document::font_reading_tests` in `document_changed_set_tests.rs` and `document_font_reading_tests.rs` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3729-3731; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3733-3735) and escher-driver's `mcp::tests` and `schema::tests` in `mcp_tests.rs` and `schema_tests.rs` (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:291-293; packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:540-542), each moved out whole with its test paths unchanged;
 each integration test file covers one behavior and opens with a `//!` doc naming the behavior and any guarded bug (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:1-7); regression tests cite upstream issue or PR URLs (tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_interaction_state.rs:5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:3); documents built with `HtmlDocument::from_html` and a `DocumentConfig` with a `ColorScheme::Light` viewport and `HtmlProvider`, then `resolve(0.0)` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:139-145; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:14-25); scenarios run in both layout modes `for incremental in [false, true]` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:92-101; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:85-99); descriptive snake_case test names (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:32; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:39); `#[track_caller]` assertion helpers (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:40-41); some tests use `test_that` matchers returning `TestResult<()>` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:6; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:9-25); a pointer-event builder is repeated per file (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:43-62; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:45-64;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:13-32), while the seven_guis stand checks state the tables and helpers they share once, in the module `tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs`, which a check reads by declaring `mod common;` — a module in a subdirectory of the integration-test directory is no test target, so each test-target file still covers one behavior (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:1-6) — and the checks that hold a `Session` — the session checks, the settle check `stand_settle`, the fifteen driver-action checks `stand_act_*`, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `stand_mcp_tools`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `stand_screenshot_repeat` and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the driver sweep `stand_requirement_sweep` — keep what they share in a second such module, `tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs`, read by `mod session_common;` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:1-7); tests first assert the fixture produces the condition under test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:50-55; tests/blitz-tests/tests/interaction_state_canonicalization.rs:76-91); WPT test names use forward slashes relative to WPT_DIR (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:621-625); the CI Python tests use `unittest` with one `TestCase` per function (.github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:4; .github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:104-174); blitz-tests keeps one test target per file directly under `tests/` — its `[package]` sets no `autotests` — and the one file there that is declared and never built is upstream's single-binary `tests/all.rs`, the manifest's one `[[test]]` table, held at `test = false`: the operator's decision of 2026-10-10, a standing two-line difference from upstream's manifest that `BlitzTestsTargetsTest` pins (tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:46-59; .github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:17-26)
